WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.762
Let us close Module 5 by connecting the main ideas
AND OR

00:00:04.962 --> 00:00:08.212
and NOT build compound rules but mixed conditions
should be grouped with

00:00:08.225 --> 00:00:13.512
parentheses so the intended logic is visible SQL
uses TRUE FALSE and

00:00:13.538 --> 00:00:17.500
UNKNOWN and WHERE keeps only TRUE NULL is not the
same as

00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:22.500
zero or blank text Use IS NULL for missingness
Boolean predicates for

00:00:22.525 --> 00:00:25.838
nullable true and false fields and IS DISTINCT FROM
when you need

00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:31.062
a definite comparison involving NULL NULLIF can
normalize sentinel values such as

00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:36.300
blank text or zero denominators COALESCE can choose
the first available fallback

00:00:36.325 --> 00:00:40.900
when the fallback reflects a documented rule CASE
evaluates from top to

00:00:40.925 --> 00:00:46.750
bottom so specific overlapping branches belong
before broad ones Finally validate

00:00:46.775 --> 00:00:47.538
edge cases
